# K8 selective persistent-window zeroing release spec.
#
# Source combination = the 2026-08-08 latest-source spec plus the two K8
# landing commits (nothing else moved):
#   pypto      8e92b468 -> 1c048a74   distributed_runner.py +174/-22
#                                     (reset trace + selective memset)
#   pypto-lib  27a43f6a -> cb96747e   decode_fwd.py +11/-7
#                                     (7 control buffers -> window prefix)
#
# Measured on 0162 before landing (source overlay, A/B/A double bracket):
#   whole-net BS1 ctx=65536 ITL p50  33.84 -> 32.08 ms  (-1.7455 ms / -5.16%)
#   _reset_persistent_domains body   2253  -> 518 us
#   hidden_sha256 567b206bb03d89f84020e1dddd61098a8f79f32f81b8f4fcf56443113e27f03e
#   tail token 14371  (byte-exact vs production baseline)
#
# Built 2026-08-11 on the devbox; verified on 0162 digest-only.
#   manifest sha256:076af8a167405d5d0831e234cd16521c77d8bfdd173eff063d820802057c47f3
#   config   sha256:a9d111880883cea0b02e425fdfeaccc2b14bb1d1174c0b73488d8ee6d8004d39
# 0162 gates that PASSED:
#   audit + smoke (IMAGE_IMMUTABLE_AUDIT / CANONICAL_ONLY_SYMBOL_AUDIT /
#                  K8_LANDING_PRESENT / [smoke])
#   byte-exact hidden_sha256 567b206b... == production baseline, token 14371
#   N=128 predefined-oracle x3: 123/128 = 96.09375%, tp_spread_max 0.0
#   clean ITL bs=1 ctx=65536 p50 32.14 ms  (pre-K8 33.84 -> -5.02%)
# NOT re-run on this image (so it is NOT full production release-qualified):
#   Main batch16, MTP batch1/batch16, the six-BS 64K golden/A-B matrix,
#   formal matched-source DFX.  The full-matrix fallback baseline is still Wave5.
# Evidence: benchmark/2026-08-11-k8-selective-window-zeroing-image.md
#
# Build with (devbox that has docker; 0162 has no buildkit and no GitHub or
# proxy egress, so the build structurally cannot run there):
